{"name":"Lyrabar","status":"ok","title":"Lyrabar","pageId":36517,"html":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p class=\"mw-empty-elt\">\n</p><aside role=\"region\" class=\"portable-infobox pi-background pi-border-color pi-theme-frwiki pi-layout-default type-location\">\n\n\n<h2 class=\"pi-item pi-item-spacing pi-title pi-secondary-background\" data-source=\"name\">Lyrabar</h2>\n<section class=\"pi-item pi-group pi-border-color\">\n\t<h2 class=\"pi-item pi-header pi-secondary-font pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-background\">Geography</h2>\n\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"type\">\n\t\n\t\t<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Type</h3>\n\t\n\t<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\">Capital city</div>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"region\">\n\t\n\t\t<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Region</h3>\n\t\n\t<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\"><a href=\"/wiki/Easting_Coast\" title=\"Easting Coast\">Easting Coast</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Impiltur\" title=\"Impiltur\">Impiltur</a></div>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"size\">\n\t\n\t\t<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Size</h3>\n\t\n\t<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\">Metropolis</div>\n</div>\n\n</section>\n<section class=\"pi-item pi-group pi-border-color\">\n\t<h2 class=\"pi-item pi-header pi-secondary-font pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-background\">Society<sup id=\"cite_ref-Rage-p?_1-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-Rage-p?-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></h2>\n\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"religion\">\n\t\n\t\t<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Religions</h3>\n\t\n\t<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\"><a href=\"/wiki/Sel%C3%BBne\" title=\"Selûne\">Selûne</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Sune\" title=\"Sune\">Sune</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/The_Triad\" title=\"The Triad\">the Triad</a></div>\n</div>\n\n</section>\n<h2 class=\"pi-item pi-header pi-secondary-font pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-background\">History<sup id=\"cite_ref-FRCS3e-p203_2-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-FRCS3e-p203-2\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>2<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup><sup id=\"cite_ref-FRCG-p144_3-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-FRCG-p144-3\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>3<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></h2>\n<section class=\"pi-item pi-group pi-border-color\">\n\t\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"population1\">\n\t\n\t\t<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Population</h3>\n\t\n\t<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\">50,000&#160;in <a href=\"/wiki/1479_DR\" title=\"1479 DR\">1479&#160;DR</a><br>52,305&#160;in <a href=\"/wiki/1372_DR\" title=\"1372 DR\">1372&#160;DR</a></div>\n</div>\n\n</section>\n<nav class=\"pi-navigation pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-font\"><a href=\"/wiki/Category:Inhabitants_of_Lyrabar\" title=\"Category:Inhabitants of Lyrabar\">Inhabitants of  Lyrabar</a></nav>\n<nav class=\"pi-navigation pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-font\"><a href=\"/wiki/Category:Locations_in_Lyrabar\" title=\"Category:Locations in Lyrabar\">Locations in  Lyrabar</a></nav>\n<nav class=\"pi-navigation pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-font\"><a href=\"/wiki/Category:Organizations_in_Lyrabar\" class=\"newcategory\" title=\"Category:Organizations in Lyrabar\">Organizations in  Lyrabar</a></nav>\n</aside>\n\n<p class=\"mw-empty-elt\"></p><p><b>Lyrabar</b>, previously known as <b>Impil's Tor</b>, was a great port-city that served as the capital of <a href=\"/wiki/Impiltur\" title=\"Impiltur\">Impiltur</a> from the 13<sup>th</sup> until the 16<sup>th</sup> century <a href=\"/wiki/DR\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"DR\">DR</a>.<sup id=\"cite_ref-D346.I_4-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-D346.I-4\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>4<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup><sup id=\"cite_ref-HoF-p61_5-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-HoF-p61-5\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>5<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup> It boasted some of the most grand and beautiful builds of the realm, including the <span class=\"new\" title=\"Royal Palace (Lyrabar) (page does not exist)\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvUm95YWxfUGFsYWNlXyhMeXJhYmFyKT9hY3Rpb249ZWRpdCZyZWRsaW5rPTE=\">Royal Palace</span> and the <span class=\"new\" title=\"Tower Pureheart (page does not exist)\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvVG93ZXJfUHVyZWhlYXJ0P2FjdGlvbj1lZGl0JnJlZGxpbms9MQ==\">tower</span> of the <a href=\"/wiki/Lords_of_Imphras_II\" title=\"Lords of Imphras II\">Lords of Imphras II</a>.<sup id=\"cite_ref-D346.I_4-1\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-D346.I-4\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>4<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\"><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Description\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Description</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Trade\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Trade</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Defense\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Defense</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#History\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">History</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Notable_Locations\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Notable Locations</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Appendix\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Appendix</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#References\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">References</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Description\">Description</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a title=\"Edit section: Description\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" data-action=\"edit-section\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Lyrabar?veaction=edit&section=1\" aria-label=\"Edit section: Description\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The city was long and narrow, stretching over a mile along the northern coast of the <a href=\"/wiki/Sea_of_Fallen_Stars\" title=\"Sea of Fallen Stars\">Sea of Fallen Stars</a>.<sup id=\"cite_ref-FRCS3e-p203_2-1\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-FRCS3e-p203-2\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>2<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup><sup id=\"cite_ref-FRCG-p144_3-1\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-FRCG-p144-3\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>3<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p><p>Prior to the <a href=\"/wiki/1385_DR\" title=\"1385 DR\">Year of Blue Fire, 1385 DR</a>, the city had no slums or impoverished quarter. The <a href=\"/wiki/Priest\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Priest\">priests</a> of <a href=\"/wiki/Ilmater\" title=\"Ilmater\">Ilmater</a> tended to the poorer citizens of Impiltur's large cities and maintained their social welfare.<sup id=\"cite_ref-D346.I_4-2\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-D346.I-4\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>4<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Trade\">Trade</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a title=\"Edit section: Trade\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" data-action=\"edit-section\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Lyrabar?veaction=edit&section=2\" aria-label=\"Edit section: Trade\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Lyrabar was home to one of the <a href=\"/wiki/Thayan_enclave\" title=\"Thayan enclave\">trade enclaves</a> operated by the <a href=\"/wiki/Red_Wizards\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Red Wizards\">Red Wizards</a> of <a href=\"/wiki/Thay\" title=\"Thay\">Thay</a>.<sup id=\"cite_ref-UE-p191_6-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-UE-p191-6\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>6<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup><sup id=\"cite_ref-D346.I_4-3\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-D346.I-4\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>4<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p><p>The city was renowned for its many rival sailing academies, at least one of which (<span class=\"new\" title=\"Waywater's Nautical University (page does not exist)\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvV2F5d2F0ZXIlMjdzX05hdXRpY2FsX1VuaXZlcnNpdHk/YWN0aW9uPWVkaXQmcmVkbGluaz0x\">Waywater's Nautical University</span>) was known for teaching <a href=\"/wiki/Abjuration\" title=\"Abjuration\">abjuration</a> <a href=\"/wiki/Magic\" title=\"Magic\">magic</a> useful for ships' <a href=\"/wiki/Mage\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Mage\">mages</a>.<sup id=\"cite_ref-HoF-p61_5-1\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-HoF-p61-5\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>5<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Defense\">Defense</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a title=\"Edit section: Defense\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" data-action=\"edit-section\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Lyrabar?veaction=edit&section=3\" aria-label=\"Edit section: Defense\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>The city housed a large fleet of ships, both military and mercantile. The port was well-protected by the royal warships.<sup id=\"cite_ref-FRCS3e-p203_2-2\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-FRCS3e-p203-2\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>2<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p><p>On land, the city was the headquarters of the <a href=\"/wiki/Warswords\" title=\"Warswords\">Warswords</a>, who were responsible for patrolling the trade routes of Impiltur. They were known to sometimes deputize <a href=\"/wiki/Adventurer\" title=\"Adventurer\">adventurers</a> as \"swordpoints\".<sup id=\"cite_ref-HoF-p61_5-2\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-HoF-p61-5\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>5<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"History\">History</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a title=\"Edit section: History\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" data-action=\"edit-section\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Lyrabar?veaction=edit&section=4\" aria-label=\"Edit section: History\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The settlement of Impil's Tor was originally founded by <span class=\"new\" title=\"Impil Mirandor (page does not exist)\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvSW1waWxfTWlyYW5kb3I/YWN0aW9uPWVkaXQmcmVkbGluaz0x\">Impil Mirandor</span> in the <a href=\"/wiki/135_DR\" title=\"135 DR\">Year of Old Beginnings, -135 DR</a>, atop the ancient <a href=\"/wiki/Dwarf\" title=\"Dwarf\">dwarfhold</a> of <span class=\"new\" title=\"Felimar (page does not exist)\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvRmVsaW1hcj9hY3Rpb249ZWRpdCZyZWRsaW5rPTE=\">Felimar</span>. The founder Impil was a refugee who fled the fall of ancient <a href=\"/wiki/Jhaamdath\" title=\"Jhaamdath\">Jhaamdath</a>. The fledgling settlement was renamed Lyrabar by Impil's son <span class=\"new\" title=\"Ornrath Mirandor (page does not exist)\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvT3JucmF0aF9NaXJhbmRvcj9hY3Rpb249ZWRpdCZyZWRsaW5rPTE=\">Ornrath</span>, in the <a href=\"/wiki/-118_DR\" title=\"-118 DR\">Year of Elven Delights, -118 DR</a>, who proceeded to open up trade agreements with the nearby <a href=\"/wiki/Dwarven\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Dwarven\">dwarven</a> settlements.<sup id=\"cite_ref-GHotR-p57_7-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-GHotR-p57-7\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>7<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p><p>In the <a href=\"/wiki/1295_DR\" title=\"1295 DR\">Year of the Ormserpent, 1295 DR</a>, the capital city of <a href=\"/wiki/Dilpur\" title=\"Dilpur\">Dilpur</a> was sacked during the <span class=\"new\" title=\"Prince's Revolt (page does not exist)\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvUHJpbmNlJTI3c19SZXZvbHQ/YWN0aW9uPWVkaXQmcmVkbGluaz0x\">Prince's Revolt</span>. When <a href=\"/wiki/Rilimbrar\" title=\"Rilimbrar\">King Rilimbrar</a> assumed the throne that year, he established Lyrabar as new capital of the re-established kingdom.<sup id=\"cite_ref-D346.I_4-4\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-D346.I-4\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>4<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p><p>When the Spellplague struck in 1385 DR and the <a href=\"/wiki/Sea_of_Fallen_Stars\" title=\"Sea of Fallen Stars\">Sea of Fallen Stars</a> receded, the city's port was left dry, disrupting trade until the port was rebuilt closer to the water.  Lyrabar was known for its criminal organizations, which made secret arrangements with the city guard.<sup id=\"cite_ref-FRCG-p144_3-2\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-FRCG-p144-3\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>3<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p><p>After the waters of Sea of Fallen Stars <a href=\"/wiki/Great_Rain\" title=\"Great Rain\">rose again</a> following the <a href=\"/wiki/Second_Sundering\" title=\"Second Sundering\">Second Sundering</a>, Lyrabar's fortunes (along with those of Impiltur as a whole) rose with them.<sup id=\"cite_ref-HoF-p61_5-3\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-HoF-p61-5\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>5<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Notable_Locations\">Notable Locations</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a title=\"Edit section: Notable Locations\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" data-action=\"edit-section\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Lyrabar?veaction=edit&section=5\" aria-label=\"Edit section: Notable Locations\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<dl><dt>Landmarks</dt>\n<dd></dd></dl>\n<ul><li>Royal Gaols: The city was home to one the several prisons that harbored criminals of the realm.<sup id=\"cite_ref-D346.I_4-5\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-D346.I-4\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>4<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></li>\n<li><span class=\"new\" title=\"Royal Palace (Lyrabar) (page does not exist)\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvUm95YWxfUGFsYWNlXyhMeXJhYmFyKT9hY3Rpb249ZWRpdCZyZWRsaW5rPTE=\">Royal Palace</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"new\" title=\"Tower Pureheart (page does not exist)\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvVG93ZXJfUHVyZWhlYXJ0P2FjdGlvbj1lZGl0JnJlZGxpbms9MQ==\">Tower Pureheart</span></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/Towers_of_the_Wind\" title=\"Towers of the Wind\">Towers of the Wind</a></li>\n<li><span class=\"new\" title=\"Waywater's Nautical University (page does not exist)\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvV2F5d2F0ZXIlMjdzX05hdXRpY2FsX1VuaXZlcnNpdHk/YWN0aW9uPWVkaXQmcmVkbGluaz0x\">Waywater's Nautical University</span></li></ul>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Appendix\">Appendix</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a title=\"Edit section: Appendix\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" data-action=\"edit-section\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Lyrabar?veaction=edit&section=6\" aria-label=\"Edit section: Appendix\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"References\">References</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a title=\"Edit section: References\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" data-action=\"edit-section\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Lyrabar?veaction=edit&section=7\" aria-label=\"Edit section: References\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<div class=\"reflist\">\n<div class=\"mw-references-wrap\"><ol class=\"references\">\n<li id=\"cite_note-Rage-p?-1\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><a href=\"#cite_ref-Rage-p?_1-0\">↑</a></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><a href=\"/wiki/Richard_Lee_Byers\" title=\"Richard Lee Byers\">Richard Lee Byers</a>&#160;(April 2004). <i><a href=\"/wiki/The_Rage\" title=\"The Rage\">The Rage</a></i>. (<a href=\"/wiki/Wizards_of_the_Coast\" title=\"Wizards of the Coast\">Wizards of the Coast</a>), p.&#160;?. ISBN&#160;<a href=\"/wiki/Special:BookSources/0-7869-3187-6\" title=\"Special:BookSources/0-7869-3187-6\">0-7869-3187-6</a>.</span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite_note-FRCS3e-p203-2\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\">↑ <sup><a href=\"#cite_ref-FRCS3e-p203_2-0\">2.0</a></sup> <sup><a href=\"#cite_ref-FRCS3e-p203_2-1\">2.1</a></sup> <sup><a href=\"#cite_ref-FRCS3e-p203_2-2\">2.2</a></sup></span> <spa